    "id": "unified-example-general-experience",
    "name": "Experience from confirmed scene events",
    "description": "Use generic State Progression, an authored reward table, canonical event identity and schema-aware file replacement to track experience.\n\nSetup: Create public JSON player-progression as {values:[{key:\"experience\",value:80}],ledger:[]}. Author reward rules and canonical IDs for your campaign. Bind Prose for evidence extraction and decision for each actual completion. A new event identity can earn a reward; retry cannot. The example uses generic State/Collection/Format/Write nodes, with no XP-specific operation.\n\nInspect: On Send owns this generation. Generate Reply uses the ordinary SillyTavern connection. Auxiliary roles remain unassigned in this portable example. Review the final narrative and proposed consequences; Apply publishes a new swipe and settles staged writes. Preview and bounded runs never settle.\n\nGenerated suggestions are proposals. Quoted observations preserve source identity; notes never establish canonical events. Private records cannot be appended to public notes.",
